## Context

Reading-2 findings 18, 39, 42 (tracker 0578) form one narrative
thread — screening without a reference:

- (18) Drop Annex E (sec:annex-screen, main.tex L2483–2541): it
  repeats with weak statistical power what Figure 5 shows better.
- (39) §7.2 (sec:ext-screen, L882) should refer to Figure 5
  (fig:reliability), not Annex E. Message: scores without reference
  correlate with precision → we can detect bad models and screen them
  out. Then introduce the Admiralty grading: consider models as
  information sources, runs as information packages. Note that model
  quality scoring could be useful for fusion.
- (42) Conclusion: drop "and the evidence points toward a conjecture
  about why: the binding constraint is the data, not the model. Each
  claim in that sentence rests on a measured result." — vague
  generality. Replace with evidence: with data, Mistral Large works as
  well as Opus → we may hope to solve this task without an arms race,
  via a sourcing pipeline ("On n'a pas de GPU mais on a des idées").

These must land together: the Annex E refs (L907 in sec:ext-screen,
L1250 in the Conclusion) and the rho-caveat test couple all three.

